# PT6: the dual certificate of `⌊a b / 97⌋`, real part

Source: `review/flat_spectrum.md`, *What a part of the table determines*, PT6. The upper triangle of
a symmetric matrix `Z`, row by row, in fields of 13 bits, each shifted up by 4096. The entries are
the rounded polar factor of the kernel, in units of `2⁻¹³`. They are a hint: nothing is assumed
about them, and the kernel of Lean checks what the proof needs in `TablePart.E6FloorDual`.
-/

